# Task 5 - Capstone Project

## Web Application Penetration Testing Using DVWA

For my final project, I performed security testing on DVWA (Damn Vulnerable Web Application) in my local authorized lab environment.

## Objective

The main objective was to understand common web application vulnerabilities and learn how security testing can help identify them.

## Lab Environment

- Kali Linux
- Metasploitable 2
- DVWA
- Burp Suite
- Firefox

## Vulnerabilities Practiced

- SQL Injection
- Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
- Command Execution
- File Inclusion
- CSRF
- Brute Force
- File Upload

## Security Testing

I used Burp Suite to capture and modify HTTP requests and responses.

I also used different inputs in DVWA to understand how vulnerable web applications can be attacked.

## Findings

The testing showed that insecure input handling and weak security controls can allow attackers to perform unauthorized actions or access sensitive information.

## Recommendations

- Validate user input
- Use parameterized queries
- Implement proper authentication
- Use secure session management
- Apply security headers
- Keep software updated
- Follow secure coding practices

## Learning Outcome

This project helped me understand the basic process of web application penetration testing, vulnerability identification and security recommendations.

## Conclusion

The capstone project helped me combine the cybersecurity concepts and practical skills I learned during the internship.

All testing was performed only in an authorized educational lab environment.
